GIT COMMIT
==========

Save your changes permanently.


BASIC
-----
git commit -m "Your message here"

Always describe what you changed.


OPTIONS
-------
Quick commit all changes:
  git commit -am "Message"

Opens editor for long message:
  git commit


GOOD MESSAGES
-------------
✓ "Fix login bug"
✓ "Add user profile page"
✗ "changes"
✗ "stuff"


WHAT IT DOES
------------
• Saves staged changes
• Creates a snapshot
• Records who and when
• Adds to project history


ERRORS
------
"nothing to commit"     → Run git add first
"please tell me who"    → Set git config
